From 0df4345eab43d0ddd5c05fe42e631d8fb6586b7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-rg35xx <build@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:01:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] atc260x_cap_gauge: port the installed vendor gauge build,
 safe to build in

The installed atc260x_cap_gauge.ko is a newer vendor build than the tree's source. Recovered from its
disassembly (same instructions per function, .rodata/.data byte-identical):
- battery temperature reader for the charger (act260x_set_get_temp_point): DTS support_battery_temperature
  and bat_temp_channel (default REMCON), ADC -> C table; off on the RG35XX DTS (reads -1000, ignored)
- full_power_schedule: the charger is stopped for the OCV check only at the taper voltage
- notcharging_process: OCV always measured; shown full with OCV < 4150 mV -> 99% so the charger tops up
- calc_charge_resistor: on a failed measurement restore the charge current / turn the charger back on;
  the low-current branch no longer sets the current
- get_responding_ocv: ocv_finded starts at 0; log lines re-enabled
Built in: late_initcall_sync (after the charger's late_initcall, whose hooks drop callbacks before its
probe) and no THIS_MODULE dereference.
---
 drivers/power/atc260x_cap_gauge.c | 150 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 136 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/atc260x_cap_gauge.c b/drivers/power/atc260x_cap_gauge.c
index 37b9636e..6efc6252 100755
--- a/drivers/power/atc260x_cap_gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/atc260x_cap_gauge.c
